The fmt include is written for packman's target-deps layout, where the fmt
dependency is the fmt repository itself and the header therefore sits one
directory below the repository root. The `fmt` module exports fmt's own include
directory, which is the sane thing for it to export. The translation unit
already asks for FMT_HEADER_ONLY, so only the headers are involved either way.

--- a/source/extensions/omni.kit.loop-isaac/plugins/omni.kit.loop/RunLoopRunner.cpp
+++ b/source/extensions/omni.kit.loop-isaac/plugins/omni.kit.loop/RunLoopRunner.cpp
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@

 #define FMT_HEADER_ONLY 1
 #include "RunLoopSynchronizer.h"
-#include "fmt/include/fmt/format.h"
+#include <fmt/format.h>

 static constexpr char kAppRunLoops[] = "/app/runLoops";
 static constexpr char kSyncToPresentGlobal[] = "/app/runLoopsGlobal/syncToPresent";
